{
 "summary": "A small number of checkout requests (5 sampled traces, 00:07:38Z–00:08:56Z) failed with 502 at the gateway. The errors originate in inventory POST /reserve, which returned 500 while logging 'deadlock detected'; orders and gateway only propagated it. Overall error rates stayed low (gateway avg 0.9%, max 3.4%) and latency was normal, so this looks like intermittent database deadlocks in inventory, not an outage.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Intermittent deadlocks in inventory's reservation path caused POST /reserve to return 500. Orders then returned 502 and gateway POST /checkout returned 502. The failures were fast (14–38ms), so this is not a timeout cascade.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-19d7f31f2517",
   "ev-7b87ce3c8b85",
   "ev-d2f554a49364",
   "ev-095eb88a2809"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders does not absorb inventory reservation failures. It converts each inventory 500 directly into a 502 to its caller.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-d2f554a49364",
    "ev-19d7f31f2517"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:07:38Z",
   "event": "First failing checkout. Inventory logs 'deadlock detected', orders logs that the inventory reservation failed with 500, and gateway logs that checkout failed with a 502 from orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7b87ce3c8b85",
    "ev-d2f554a49364",
    "ev-095eb88a2809",
    "ev-19d7f31f2517"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:08:56Z",
   "event": "Last observed deadlock and checkout failure in the logs and sampled traces.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7b87ce3c8b85",
    "ev-19d7f31f2517"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:09:13.447Z",
   "event": "The 5xx ratio for inventory (max 5.3%) and orders (max 6.7%) first reaches the 5% threshold.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-da4f27b25849",
    "ev-c322de0f0330"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway or orders as the origin: both only report a downstream status (502 from orders, 500 from inventory), and the error path ends at inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-19d7f31f2517",
    "ev-095eb88a2809",
    "ev-d2f554a49364"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Latency or timeout cascade: failing traces completed in 14–38ms, no service had a p95 latency onset, and inventory p95 stayed around 46ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-19d7f31f2517",
    "ev-da4f27b25849",
    "ev-c322de0f0330",
    "ev-0d8694989d39"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "No deployment records were returned for the window, so it cannot be confirmed whether inventory 3.1.5 or any other release changed recently.",
  "The deadlock log does not say which tables or locks were involved. Database-side metrics and deadlock reports are not in the snapshot.",
  "Whether the deadlocks are still occurring after the window, and whether load or concurrent reservations of the same SKU trigger them, is unknown."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Inspect the inventory database deadlock reports for the failing traces (e.g. dfd268889a3a2dfb7d9c5db170426b6f) and review the lock ordering in the POST /reserve transaction.",
   "rationale": "Inventory logged 'deadlock detected' in the same traces that failed checkout.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7b87ce3c8b85",
    "ev-19d7f31f2517"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check deployment and change history for inventory outside the deployment index, such as a release 3.1.5 rollout or schema changes.",
   "rationale": "The deployment source returned nothing for the window, so a recent change cannot be confirmed or excluded.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Consider adding a bounded retry on deadlock errors in inventory reserve, or in orders on an inventory 500.",
   "rationale": "The failures are transient and fast, and orders currently passes each one straight through to the user.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-d2f554a49364",
    "ev-19d7f31f2517"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Keep monitoring the inventory and orders error ratios to see whether the 5% threshold breach persists.",
   "rationale": "Both crossed 5% at 00:09:13Z, at the end of the window.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-da4f27b25849",
    "ev-c322de0f0330"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
